'''war-flail''' (wâr′flāl), ''n.'' A weapon used in middle ages, resembling the agricultural in its general character. {{smaller|Sometimes it was to the end of which a strong bag of leather was se by a thong, or by rings of metal. The bag seems to been stuffed with sand. Compare ''sand-bag'', ''sand-clu'' see Shakspere’s 2 Hen. VI., iv. 3. See also cut ''morning-star''.}}

